course: dictionary
lesson: 15790
title: Unaddressed: two meanings from context
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Unaddressed is a long word, but you can break it into parts. The un- part means not, and addressed can mean dealt with or having an address written on it. The context tells you which meaning fits. «The letter was unaddressed, so the postman could not deliver it.» A letter with no address cannot be delivered, so unaddressed means it has no address written on it.
explain: «The problem of the broken bridge remains unaddressed.» Nobody has fixed the bridge yet, so unaddressed means not dealt with, solved or talked about yet. Always ask: what would fit here? Then try your meaning in the sentence and check that it still makes sense.
explain: Words in stories can carry feelings too. «Sam's worry stayed unaddressed, and it grew bigger each night.» Sam never talked about his worry or fixed it, so it kept growing. Unaddressed problems often get bigger until someone faces them.
fact: Unaddressed means not dealt with, solved or talked about yet.
fact: An unaddressed letter or parcel has no address written on it.
fact: The prefix un- means not, so unaddressed is the opposite of addressed in the sense of dealt with.
fact: You can use unaddressed for problems, as in «an unaddressed problem», or for things like letters.
fact: A good check is to swap your meaning into the sentence: "not dealt with yet" or "with no address" should fit.
exercise: «The letter was unaddressed, so the postman could not deliver it.» What does unaddressed mean here? | Opened and read by everyone | Sent by a good friend | *With no address written on it | Very long and full of news
exercise: «The problem of the broken bridge remains unaddressed.» What does unaddressed suggest? | *Nobody has dealt with it yet | It has been solved and everyone is happy | It is a very big bridge | It was painted red
exercise: In unaddressed, what does the un- part mean? | Under | Very | *Not | Again
test: «Sam's worry stayed unaddressed, and it grew bigger each night.» What does unaddressed mean here? | Shared with the whole class | Solved by his mum | Written in neat handwriting | *Not dealt with yet
test: Ella finds a parcel with no name or street on it. Which word fits best? | *Unaddressed | Ancient | Luminous | Glum
exam: «The school council left the litter problem unaddressed for a whole term.» What does unaddressed mean? | Put into a box ready to post | Written neatly on a card | Thrown away in the bin | *Ignored and not yet dealt with
